# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Send It — Environment Variable Template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the real values.
# NEVER commit `.env` — it is already in .gitignore.
#
# Note: In Expo, only variables prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ are inlined
# into the JS bundle and therefore visible to the client at runtime.
# The Supabase anon key and PostHog project key are safe to ship in
# a public client bundle (they are designed for public exposure) —
# but RLS policies MUST enforce all access control in Postgres.
#
# NEVER put the Supabase service_role key in this file — it belongs
# only in Edge Function environment variables (managed via
# `supabase secrets set` on the hosted project).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase (hosted) ──
# Get from https://app.supabase.com → your project → Settings → API
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-public-key

# ── PostHog ──
# Get from https://app.posthog.com → Project Settings → Project API Key
EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_API_KEY=phc_your_project_api_key
EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
# Use https://eu.i.posthog.com if you created the project in the EU region.

# ── Expo Push (client) ──
# Optional. Expo's push service does not require a client-side key for sending.
# The Expo Access Token (below) is only needed by the Edge Function that
# calls Expo's send API server-side. Do not put an access token here.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Edge Function secrets (NOT loaded by the client — set separately)
# Set these on the Supabase project via:
#     supabase secrets set EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN=... SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=...
# Listed here only for reference so you know what the notifications
# Edge Function will need.
#
#   EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN            — from https://expo.dev/accounts/[you]/settings/access-tokens
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY    — from Supabase Settings → API (KEEP SECRET)
#   APNS_KEY_ID                  — only if you upload your own APNs key to Expo (optional)
#   APNS_TEAM_ID                 — Apple Developer team ID
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
